{"description":"Demo and sample rows (tour fixtures, the docs-demo seed, DEMO_* accounts, Bubble-era onboarding Sample Job engagements) are always excluded (DEV-2924). Read the privacy-safe candidate dossier linked to an OpenTrain proposal: masked profile, proposal summary, AI-interview summary, verification verdicts (incl. identity assurance and current-location decision detail), factual engagement disposition, neutral links, and review/contract roll-ups with a stable asOf timestamp plus explicit availability/missing/redactions/provenance metadata. Optional strict evidence:\"full\" (DEV-2923) adds ten bounded metadata-only evidence families (cap 25 items each, truthful truncation, typed continuation); omitted means concise with evidence null. Requires candidate_dossier:read scope, the default-off candidate-dossier agent surface, and a claimed account. Hidden or banned candidates read as not found; contact details, raw resumes, government IDs, message bodies/participants, provider/session references, and assessment contents or runtime internals (including cross-buyer private assessments) are never returned, and full evidence carries no compensation amounts and no coordinates/IP/ASN/timezone data. Candidate-authored free text (profile fields and the AI-interview summary) is sanitized with explicit [REDACTED_*] placeholders recorded as PRIVACY_MASKED redactions.\nCandidateProjectEligibility is a stored job-scoped participation summary, separate from person-level identity, time-bounded currentLocation, proposal-time location snapshots, and screening results. null means no participation record is available, not eligible. evaluatedAt is the stored decision timestamp (or last evaluation), not the time of this read; use it as the freshness signal. reasonCodes are diagnostic reasons from that decision, not independent vetoes: ELIGIBLE can coexist with FULL_ID_REQUIRED or a location REVIEW_REQUIRED result under a non-enforced policy. Reads do not reevaluate the decision's freshness or grant access; active overrides are filtered for expiry at read time, and protected writes enforce current policy. DECISION_STALE is added only by the access guard; SCOPE_NOT_FOUND, SCOPE_MISMATCH and SCOPE_USER_MISMATCH are scope-resolution errors. These four codes are not emitted in this read. Always inspect identity, currentLocation and reasons separately; never infer verified identity, fresh location or permission to hire/work from this summary alone.\nELIGIBLE: The stored job-participation decision allows participation and the participation is not ON_HOLD. This is not proof of verified identity or current location: a non-enforced (including SHADOW) policy records allowed=true even when reasons identify unmet requirements.\nON_HOLD: The stored participation is ON_HOLD and no active override is projected. Do not treat it as cleared for protected work; follow the canonical hold/review flow.\nINELIGIBLE: No active override or ON_HOLD state is projected, and the current decision is missing or records allowed=false. This is a job-scoped participation result, not a hiring-quality verdict or a permanent ban.\nOVERRIDE_ACTIVE: An unrevoked, unexpired participation override exists. It takes precedence in this summary, but can be action-scoped; it is not blanket permission and does not turn identity or location into verified evidence.\nreasonCodes catalog (diagnostic, not provider error strings):\nCURRENT_LOCATION_ALLOWED: Current credible location evidence satisfies the job location policy.\nCURRENT_LOCATION_OUTSIDE_ALLOWED_COUNTRIES: Credible current evidence is outside the allowed countries; confidence/repetition determines review versus a confirmed mismatch. This requires OpenTrain review: contact OpenTrain support, and the worker must supply new evidence.\nCLIENT_RESTRICTED_COUNTRY: Credible current evidence places the person in a client-restricted country. Seek human review of disputed evidence; do not bypass the client restriction.\nCLIENT_RESTRICTED_REGION: Credible current evidence places the person in a client-restricted region. Seek human review of disputed evidence; do not bypass the client restriction.\nANONYMIZED_OR_AMBIGUOUS_SIGNAL: Current network/location evidence is anonymized or ambiguous and cannot establish allowed physical presence. Ask the worker to sign in to the OpenTrain app from their current location without a VPN or proxy. Under a non-enforced policy the status stays ELIGIBLE and this code is diagnostic; the decision re-evaluates on the next signal from the worker once hired, or at the next job action while still recruiting. Under an enforced policy this decision has already opened a location hold that a new signal does not clear on its own, so contact OpenTrain support for review once the worker has signed in.\nCONFLICTING_CURRENT_SIGNALS: Credible current signals disagree on country alongside an outside-allowed-country signal. This requires OpenTrain review: contact OpenTrain support, and the worker must supply new evidence.\nINSUFFICIENT_CURRENT_EVIDENCE: There is not enough usable current evidence to establish location. Ask the worker to sign in to the OpenTrain app from their current location. Under a non-enforced policy the status stays ELIGIBLE and this code is diagnostic; the decision re-evaluates on the next signal from the worker once hired, or at the next job action while still recruiting. Under an enforced policy this decision has already opened a location hold that a new signal does not clear on its own, so contact OpenTrain support for review once the worker has signed in.\nSTALE_LOCATION_EVIDENCE: Recorded location observations are no longer usable as current evidence. Ask the worker to sign in to the OpenTrain app from their current location. Under a non-enforced policy the status stays ELIGIBLE and this code is diagnostic; the decision re-evaluates on the next signal from the worker once hired, or at the next job action while still recruiting. Under an enforced policy this decision has already opened a location hold that a new signal does not clear on its own, so contact OpenTrain support for review once the worker has signed in.\nACTIVE_HOLD_REQUIRES_REVIEW: An existing location hold needs explicit review/challenge; a later passive signal alone does not clear it.\nPROVIDER_EVIDENCE_UNAVAILABLE: Current provider evidence is unavailable; independent usable evidence has not established location. Wait for provider recovery or seek human review; do not treat an outage as clearance.\nFULL_ID_REQUIRED: Full identity is required by the job policy but has not been verified or requested. Request full identity verification from the proposal in the OpenTrain app; the worker then completes it. No public API or MCP operation can request it.\nFULL_ID_IN_PROGRESS: Required full identity verification is requested or in progress; it is not yet verified. Wait for the pending verification result.\nFULL_ID_FAILED: Required full identity verification failed. Seek human review before any permitted retry; do not infer clearance.\nFULL_ID_EXPIRED: Required full identity verification has expired. Re-request full identity verification.\nFULL_ID_NEEDS_REVIEW: Required full identity needs review, including a provider-approved record whose full-identity evidence is incomplete. Provider approval alone is not sufficient. Seek human identity review.\nSCOPE_NOT_FOUND: The requested job/contract/proposal participation scope could not be resolved. Scope-resolution error only; not emitted in this CandidateProjectEligibility read.\nSCOPE_MISMATCH: The supplied scope identifiers do not resolve to the same job/participation context. Scope-resolution error only; not emitted in this CandidateProjectEligibility read.\nSCOPE_USER_MISMATCH: The supplied person does not match the resolved participation scope. Scope-resolution error only; not emitted in this CandidateProjectEligibility read.\nDECISION_MISSING: The participation has no current eligibility decision; this is not evidence of clearance.\nDECISION_STALE: The decision is stale for the current policy/evidence or time window and needs reevaluation. Access-guard code only; not emitted in this CandidateProjectEligibility read. Use evaluatedAt as the freshness signal.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"evidence":{"description":"Strict evidence mode (DEV-2923): omitted means concise (evidence null in the response); \"full\" adds the ten bounded metadata-only evidence families (cap 25 items each, truthful truncation, typed continuation). Exact lowercase values only.","enum":["concise","full"],"type":"string"},"proposalId":{"description":"OpenTrain proposal (job offer) id the candidate dossier is linked to.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["proposalId"],"type":"object"},"name":"opentrain_get_candidate_dossier","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"apiBaseUrl":{"type":"string"},"result":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"dossier":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"aiInterview":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"interviewOnlyScore":{"type":["number","null"]},"score":{"type":["number","null"]},"summary":{"type":["string","null"]},"transcriptAvailable":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["score","interviewOnlyScore","summary","transcriptAvailable"],"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}]},"asOf":{"type":"string"},"availability":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"aiInterview":{"$ref":"#/properties/result/properties/dossier/properties/availability/properties/candidate"},"candidate":{"enum":["available","missing"],"type":"string"},"contractHistory":{"$ref":"#/properties/result/properties/dossier/properties/availability/properties/candidate"},"proposal":{"$ref":"#/properties/result/properties/dossier/properties/availability/properties/candidate"},"reviews":{"$re